rm-memes.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/artifical-intelligence-fakes-midterm-memes.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The surge of A.I. fakes that emerged this election season was different than what researchers had feared. The results are also a reckoning.</description><dc:creator>Stuart A. Thompson</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:13:29 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Video Recordings</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Downloads and Streaming</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">2026 Midterm Elections</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">political ad</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Campaign ad</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Rumors and Misinformation</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Comedy</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/12/business/ai-disinfo-memes/ai-disinfo-memes-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.png" medium="image"><media:credit>X</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>What Do You Want to Know About New York Times Journalism and A.I.?</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/insider/nyt-journalism-ai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/insider/nyt-journalism-ai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/insider/nyt-journalism-ai.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>New York Times journalists want to answer your questions about how we’re using artificial intelligence in our report.</description><dc:creator>Chloe W. Shakin</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:05:44 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">journalism</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">journalist</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">news media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">The New York Times</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">internal-reader-callout</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2021/04/22/business/trust-aicallout/22NYT-TECH-01-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Jeenah Moon for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>We want to hear your questions about A.I. and New York Times journalism.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Who Could Replace Jensen Huang as Nvidia’s CEO? Here Are 7 Candidates.</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-successor.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-successor.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-successor.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>President Trump suggested Tim Cook, Apple’s former C.E.O., to replace Jensen Huang at Nvidia. Here are others with experience in chips or A.I.</description><dc:creator>Don Clark</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:56:01 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computer Chip</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.